{"title":"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) #3</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems (page does not exist)\">2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) #7</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The smallest number in the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/8/2a893d0435d2d66236dfb9e46539b2cea0f17e85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\{ \\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{2}{3}, \\frac{1}{4}, \\frac{5}{6}, \\frac{7}{12} \\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"135\" height=\"45\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/3/5d3fd1cd478b998d6c8e566677be301de3249fc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{2}{3} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{1}{4} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{5}{6} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{7}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"380\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can convert all of the fractions to a common denominator, and then see which fraction has the smallest denominator. \n</p><p>We notice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/0/f7092e4644be7e8b9eafdfce28d2bc3c6fc456f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 = 2^2 \\times 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/e/29ee17d1e6210ee20fe6a4aec79fea296ec32f28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 = 2 \\times 3$\" width=\"73\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/c/fec451be937b467cb66db472e8bf738e96552f85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 = 2^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/d/53da2a02f6bb67e3a224d4f3acccf0b3bbc1b6d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 = 3$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/9/5a905158a0cc49faf19f98f4bb48d78626232626.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 = 2$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />. Thus, the common denominator is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/a/52aad305e4d8ffa1355fbc5e54fea520cc5488f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{1 \\times 2 \\times 3}{2 \\times 2 \\times 3} = \\frac{6}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"161\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/3/3f38f02044f1987a1bd76fc73c07f33963850ca5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{2 \\times 2^2}{3 \\times 2^2} = \\frac{8}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"137\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/4/db4d554ee6d33aa6e5c5ffd6c4d2eb27fcd466fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{1 \\times 3}{4 \\times 3} = \\frac{3}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"130\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/5/625cb6e0ec0f4d570288a35d2d01328ee3eba2c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{6} = \\frac{5 \\times 2}{6 \\times 2} = \\frac{10}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"130\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/9/a499daed13cb9b46980f91b9f759a0711c1e27f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7}{12} = \\frac{7 \\times 1}{12 \\times 1} = \\frac{7}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"148\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Of these fractions, the one that had the smallest numerator was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/6/5a6782e3a75e5e7b896f0d97b51ae434b9da6a1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" />, which is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/7/f776fd35a9bebeb5f8e9c0450e9611be3ba3ed17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } \\frac{1}{4}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"61\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can notice that except for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, all of the numerators of the fractions are greater than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the denominator. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/3/b73325ee77cf279db9914d2ab3d8a40c68084ad6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\times 3 = \\frac{3}{2} &lt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"117\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/7/d077e3601a4901a99c63c17f056e1dec48985ac5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\times 2 = 1 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"113\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/a/33a0e1f710fceaf8482f43187572ffe656f82d73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\times 6 = 3 &lt; 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"113\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/c/3dc8b463036941089fff0e88c89d3ee682306f86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\times 12 = 6 &lt; 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"122\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/7/f776fd35a9bebeb5f8e9c0450e9611be3ba3ed17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } \\frac{1}{4}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"61\" height=\"49\" /> is the smallest number in the set.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/1/18113d426de323db38c7feda70e4e2e7382f3675.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{2}{2} - \\frac{1}{2} = 1 - \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"156\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/1/1a1d70dc1d43da142749a6e685ae70e735a0f01e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{3}{3} - \\frac{1}{3} = 1 - \\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"156\" height=\"38\" />. This must be larger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> has a larger denominator than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, so a smaller fraction is being subtracted from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> has to be smaller than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> due to having a larger denominator\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/6/826708e89bc88dbf22484bf0c8decf2bee1e5db5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{6} = \\frac{6}{6} - \\frac{1}{6} = 1 - \\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"156\" height=\"38\" />. This must be larger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/7547747b133453d3c209cff6cfbf129aa67a6947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> using similar logic.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/c/33cc05ab78b892da639cac27adcf0f37844b1593.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7}{12} = \\frac{6}{12} + \\frac{1}{12} = \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"197\" height=\"38\" />. This must be larger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/3/b5368c35209887ef770207f53118a3e2e7f84839.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{12} &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"38\" />. \n</p><p>Putting this altogether, we can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/7/f776fd35a9bebeb5f8e9c0450e9611be3ba3ed17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } \\frac{1}{4}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"61\" height=\"49\" /> is the smallest number in the set.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 7 (page does not exist)\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 8 (page does not exist)\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 9 (page does not exist)\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 11 (page does not exist)\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 13 (page does not exist)\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems